$DIR/main.p:17:17: cannot pass the loop body to seq, which keeps it after returning
    A range loop over a function (at main.p:17) calls the function with a yield
    function whose body is the loop body, a closure built in f's frame (section
    12.11); yield may be called only while the loop runs. seq stores yield in
    package variable keepY (main.p:11), so the loop body would outlive f's
    frame.
    Go would move this memory to the heap, and its garbage collector would free
    it later. Plutonium has no garbage collector and never moves memory to the
    heap behind the program's back, so that every allocation is visible in the
    code.
    Change seq to call yield only while it runs, without keeping it (language
    spec section 12.11).
    (see "Views" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.3)
    (run "pluto explain E3003" for a longer explanation)
